# Test: show doctor on a running daemon names an environment value ze could
#       not use, with the default ze used and the corrected export.
# Spec: spec-doctor-coverage-12-plugin-infra AC-35
# VALIDATES: the env-values runtime check
#   (internal/component/doctor/checks_env_values.go) reads env.InvalidValues
#   in the daemon process, whose environment holds ze.metrics.interval set to
#   text no duration parses, and answers doctor-env-invalid-value naming the
#   key, the value, the type and the default 10s, with the export as its fix.
# PREVENTS: a mistyped export running the daemon on a default with no row on
#   the surface an operator or AI reads to debug the box.
# Why not a unit test: the units prove the record and the row; only the
#   daemon route proves the check runs in the process whose environment the
#   operator set, and not in the local ze doctor process, which never saw it.
#
# No `ze init`: the store is not part of the question, and seeding it is a
# whole ze process that was killed after 98 s under the stress run. The daemon
# starts from the file (`ze start running.conf`, as test/plugin/
# drain-show-answers.ci does) on the runner's default in-memory store, and
# authenticates the config's own user. The client takes its credentials from
# the environment, as test/policy/policy-interface-list-counters.ci does:
# ze.ssh.username and ze.ssh.password stand in for the store's super-admin
# (resolveUsername and resolvePassword, internal/component/cli/sshclient/
# client.go), and ze.ssh.port names the daemon's listener (resolveHostPort).
# No store sits in the work directory, so the client reads it as unavailable
# rather than failing (openStoreIfReadable). 127.0.0.1 needs no host-key
# check (hostKeyCallback), so ze.ssh.insecure is not set.

option=timeout:value=60s
option=env:var=ze.ssh.username:value=admin
option=env:var=ze.ssh.password:value=testpass
option=env:var=ze.ssh.port:value=$PORT
option=env:var=ze.metrics.interval:value=tenseconds
tmpfs=running.conf:terminator=EOF_CONF
system {
	authentication {
		# bcrypt cost-4 hash of "testpass".
		user admin {
			password "$2a$04$UlwuiuH82Unfsq.XEMPGJeDkXwbm3KW.nvVaVXOd/JeFK8VjMjrQO"
		}
	}
}
environment {
	ssh {
		enabled true
		server main {
			ip 127.0.0.1;
			port $PORT;
		}
	}
}
EOF_CONF

# "Ze running." is printed after the SSH server started (sshBuildStandalone
# and sshBuild run earlier in cmd/ze/hub), and its Start returns only once the
# listener accepts (serveListener, internal/component/ssh/listener_start.go).
cmd=background:seq=1:exec=ze start running.conf:name=daemon:ready=Ze running.

cmd=foreground:seq=2:exec=ze cli -c "show doctor | json":exit=0
expect=stdout:contains="code": "doctor-env-invalid-value"
expect=stdout:contains=environment variable ze.metrics.interval holds
expect=stdout:contains=tenseconds
expect=stdout:contains=which is not a valid duration
expect=stdout:contains=default 10s
expect=stdout:contains="fix": "export ZE_METRICS_INTERVAL=10s"
